              "text": "In late 2025, Comcast spun off several of its cable channels (including MSNBC) into an independent company called **Versant Media Group**. As part of this transition, **MSNBC was rebranded as \"MS NOW\"** (dropping the \"NBC\" and the peacock logo). \n\nThere is **no 100% free, legal 24/7 live video stream** of MS NOW (formerly MSNBC) available online without a subscription. While pirate streaming websites exist, they are often unsafe, full of invasive ads, and operate illegally.\n\nThe best legal, free, and low-cost ways to watch or listen to MS NOW (MSNBC) live online include:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Free Live Audio Streaming (100% Free)\nIf you just want to keep up with the news and commentators in real-time, you can listen to the **entire live broadcast for free**:\n*   **The MS NOW App:** Available for iOS and Android. The app includes a \"Listen\" tab that lets you stream the live broadcast audio 24/7 for free.\n*   **TuneIn Radio:** You can listen to the live MS NOW audio stream completely free on the TuneIn app or website. \n*   **Smart Speakers:** If you have an Amazon Echo or Google Nest, you can simply say, *\"Alexa, play MS NOW on TuneIn\"*.\n\n### 2. Watch Free Clips and Highlights (On-Demand)\nIf you don't need the continuous live feed but want to watch the main segments from your favorite shows (such as *Morning Joe*, *The Rachel Maddow Show*, or *The Beat with Ari Melber*):\n*   **YouTube:** The official **MS NOW YouTube channel** uploads major segments, interviews, and show highlights for free shortly after they air on television.\n*   **Official Website:** You can watch free, curated news video clips on **ms.now**.\n\n### 3. Log In with a TV Provider (Free if you have cable/satellite)\nIf you or a family member has a traditional cable, satellite, or live TV subscription, you can stream the channel live for free:\n1. Download the **MS NOW app** on your phone, tablet, or streaming device (Roku, Apple TV, Fire TV).\n2. Select **\"Live TV\"** and choose to sign in with your TV provider credentials. \n\n### 4. Use a Free Trial on a Live TV Streaming Service\nIf you want to watch the live video feed but don't have cable, you can sign up for a **Live TV streaming service**. Many of these services offer free trials for new users, which you can use to stream MS NOW live:\n*   **Fubo:** Often offers a 5-to-7-day free trial and includes MS NOW in its base packages.\n*   **YouTube TV:** Frequently offers a free trial and features MS NOW in its channel lineup.\n*   **DirecTV Stream:** Regularly provides a 5-day free trial that includes MS NOW.\n*   **Sling TV:** While Sling rarely offers free trials, their **Sling Blue** package is typically the most budget-friendly monthly option for streaming live news channels.\n\n### 5. Free Live News Alternative: NBC News NOW\nIf you are looking for a completely free, 24/7 live video news channel, NBCUniversal's **NBC News NOW** remains 100% free. It is a high-quality, professional live news network that you can stream without any subscription or login on platforms like Peacock, Pluto TV, Tubi, and the NBC News app.",
